 me, of some of my favorite recent albums of women in rock. So please donate, wear our station swag with pride, and I can guarantee that everyone will know that you\'re one cool cat! ♫</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":780} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Funny-Animal-Wallpaper-06-2-1024x762.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-780\"/><figcaption>A rare picture of your favorite feisty feline struggling (as usual) to get the turntables prepped and ready in time. </figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->','Cat Fight','','inherit','closed','closed','','448-revision-v1','','','2019-03-27 03:44:01','2019-03-27 03:44:01','',448,'https://telethon.wruw.org/448-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(788,51,'2019-03-27 03:45:28','2019-03-27 03:45:28','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"placeholder\":\"Content…\"} -->\n<p>Cat Fight is back for an awesome second year, and you know what that means - a second year of Telethon!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Did you know that, every week, when I\'m planning my playlists, I delve into a massive library of thousands of CDs, records, MP3s, and cassettes in search of music? It\'s every DJ\'s dream!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Such a remarkable music collection would not be possible without the continued contributions of WRUW\'s listeners. This is the one time a year that we ask you, our listeners, for help in continuing this station and everything wonderful it does - from live weekly performances and insightful public affairs shows to Studio-a-rama and other community events. Without WRUW, you wouldn\'t have the option to listen to cat-themed radio programs showcasing women in rock!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This year, I\'m setting the ambitious fundraising goal of $500 - I hope that, together with my listeners, we can meet or even surpass this goal. This year, WRUW is offering a wide range of premiums as thanks for your donation (check out those t shirts!) and I am currently in the process of securing some CD premiums, hand selected by me, of some of my favorite recent albums of women in rock. So please donate, wear our station swag with pride, and I can guarantee that everyone will know that you\'re one cool cat! ♫</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":780} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Funny-Animal-Wallpaper-06-2-1024x762.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-780\"/><figcaption>A rare picture of your favorite feisty feline struggling (as usual) to get the turntables prepped and ready in time for the broadcast. </figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->','Cat Fight','','inherit','closed','closed','','448-revision-v1','','','2019-03-27 03:45:28','2019-03-27 03:45:28','',448,'https://telethon.wruw.org/448-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(789,47,'2019-03-27 14:09:42','2019-03-27 14:09:42','Annual WRUW Telethon during Voices and Choices tuesday April 9th at 6:00 p.m.','Voices and Choices','','inherit','closed','closed','','734-revision-v1','','','2019-03-27 14:09:42','2019-03-27 14:09:42','',734,'https://telethon.wruw.org/734-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(791,47,'2019-04-09 17:33:05','2019-04-09 21:33:05','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tuesdays at 6:00 pm Voices and Choices is locally produced public affairs radio co-hosted by Dr. David Miller, Matt Hooke (CWRU \'21) and Dot Martin.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:gallery {\"ids\":[792]} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/2019-VandC-team-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"792\" data-link=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/?attachment_id=792\" class=\"wp-image-792\"/></figure></li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:gallery -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Voices and Choices','','trash','closed','closed','','voices-choices__trashed','','','2021-03-07 10:08:54','2021-03-07 15:08:54','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?page_id=791',0,'page','',0),(792,47,'2019-03-27 14:15:49','2019-03-27 14:15:49','','2019 VandC team','','inherit','open','closed','','2019-vandc-team','','','2019-03-27 14:15:49','2019-03-27 14:15:49','',791,'https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/2019-VandC-team.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(793,47,'2019-03-27 14:16:11','2019-03-27 14:16:11','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tuesdays at 6:00 pm Voices and Choices is locally produced public affairs radio co-hosted by Dr. David Miller, Matt Hooke (CWRU \'21) and Dot Martin.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:gallery {\"ids\":[792]} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/2019-VandC-team-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"792\" data-link=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/?attachment_id=792\" class=\"wp-image-792\"/></figure></li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:gallery -->','Voices and Choices','','inherit','closed','closed','','791-revision-v1','','','2019-03-27 14:16:11','2019-03-27 14:16:11','',791,'https://telethon.wruw.org/791-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(796,1,'2019-03-27 17:34:55','2019-03-27 17:34:55','','cc5177e7c50ef232cff1c8e8be7a3b82.png','','inherit','open','closed','','cc5177e7c50ef232cff1c8e8be7a3b82-png','','','2019-03-27 17:34:55','2019-03-27 17:34:55','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/cc5177e7c50ef232cff1c8e8be7a3b82.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(798,1,'2019-03-27 17:34:56','2019-03-27 17:34:56','','43b8d1e30dd544e3aa9b19775f69fc1b.png','','inherit','open','closed','','43b8d1e30dd544e3aa9b19