uploads/2019/04/IMG_0476.jpg)\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Erie Effusion','','inherit','closed','closed','','462-revision-v1','','','2019-04-07 22:02:51','2019-04-08 02:02:51','',462,'https://telethon.wruw.org/462-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3554,107,'2019-04-07 22:03:21','2019-04-08 02:03:21','<!-- wp:image {\"id\":3551} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0473.jpg\" alt=\"It\'s my face \" class=\"wp-image-3551\"/><figcaption>DJ BG </figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0476.jpg\",\"id\":3552} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim\" style=\"background-image:url(https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0476.jpg)\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->','Erie Effusion Telethon Page','','inherit','closed','closed','','462-revision-v1','','','2019-04-07 22:03:21','2019-04-08 02:03:21','',462,'https://telethon.wruw.org/462-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3556,107,'2019-04-07 22:19:13','2019-04-08 02:19:13','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hello World ! Welcome to my telethon page. This week WRUW 91.1FM is asking for your support April 8- April 14, 2019. My telethon show  will be this Sunday Sunday Sunday, April 14, from 6-8pm. Donations can be placed by calling the station at 216-368-2208, placing your donation on line WRUW.org  or sending us a check to WRUW  11220 Bellflower Road, Cleveland OH 44106. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Since 2006, I have had the pleasure, little treasure of hosting my own radio show on WRUW 91.1FM playing the Underground Eighties. Our vinyl collection is one of the largest on a college campus and perfect to pick and pull my music from obscure, rare or out of print options not available for download or digital reproduction. New wave, Brit pop, punk rock, alternative tunes, dance singles, twelve inches, seven inches, extended remixes, rare versions, soundtracks, compilations, remixes, remasters, new music from 80\'s artists and me, your hostess with the mostest every Sunday evening. I grew up in Cleveland, became a college dj on WKSR / Black Squirrel Radio 850 am and currently enjoy volunteering at the station playing my little flat friends from the 80\'s. Thank you listening, requesting and supporting my little retro radio show !  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":3551} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0473.jpg\" alt=\"It\'s my face \" class=\"wp-image-3551\"/><figcaption>DJ BG </figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0476.jpg\",\"id\":3552} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim\" style=\"background-image:url(https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/IMG_0476.jpg)\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Erie Effusion Telethon Page','','inherit','closed','closed','','462-revision-v1','','','2019-04-07 22:19:13','2019-04-08 02:19:13','',462,'https://telethon.wruw.org/462-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3561,112,'2019-04-08 00:09:20','2019-04-08 04:09:20','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; WRUW has a long and proud history presenting the music of New Orleans and Louisiana.&nbsp; In past years you could hear it on \"When the Roses Bloom Again\" with Cuzin Dave, \"Annie\'s Blues Show\" with Ann Weatherhead , \"Rhythm &amp; Blues Survey\" &amp; \"Blue Monday\" with Walking Dr. Bill Anderson and \"Chanka Chank\" with Alison Kaslow Minor (One of the people responsible for starting the New Orleans Jazz &amp; Heritage Festival) as well as other shows. &nbsp; I have learned to love this music from these programmers and Ron Cass who started \"Fat Monday.\"&nbsp; </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; Your help during the 2019 WRUW Telethon will enable us to continue this tradition by adding even more music, both old and new, to continue presenting the great music to WRUW\'s listeners. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Fat Monday','','inherit','closed','closed','','465-revision-v1','','','2019-04-08 00:09:20','2019-04-08 04:09:20','',465,'https://telethon.wruw.org/465-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3563,112,'2019-04-08 00:09:28','2019-04-08 04:09:28','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; WRUW has a long and proud history presenting the music of New Orleans and Louisiana.&nbsp; In past years you could hear it on \"When the Roses Bloom Again\" with Cuzin Dave, \"Annie\'s Blues Show\" with Ann Weatherhead , \"Rhythm &amp; Blues Survey\" &amp; \"Blue Monday\" with Walking Dr. Bill Anderson and \"Chanka Chank\" with Alison Kaslow Minor (One of the people responsible for starting the New Orleans Jazz &amp; Heritage Festival) as well as other shows. &nbsp; I have learned to love this music from these programmers and Ron Cass who started \"Fat Monday.\"&nbsp; </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; Your help during the 2019 WRUW Telethon will enable us to continue this tradition by adding even more music, both old and new, to continue presenting the great music to WRUW\'s listeners. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Fat Monday','','inherit','closed','closed','','465-revision-v1','','','2019-04-08 00:09:28','2019-04-08 04:09:28','',465,'https://telethon.wruw.org/465-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3565,112,'2019-04-08 00:10:09','2019-04-08 04:10:09','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; WRUW has a long and proud history presenting the music of New Orleans and Louisiana.&nbsp; In past years you could hear it on \"When the Roses Bloom Again\" with Cuzin Dave, \"Annie\'s Blues Show\" with Ann Weatherhead , \"Rhythm &amp; Blues Survey\" &amp; \"Blue Monday\" with Walking Dr. Bill Anderson and \"Chanka Chank\" with Alison Kaslow Minor (One of the people responsible for starting the New Orleans Jazz &amp; Heritage Festival) as well as other shows. &nbsp; I have learned to love this music from these programmers and Ron Cass who started \"Fat Monday.\"&nbsp; </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; Your help during the 2019 WRUW Telethon will enable us to continue this tradition by adding even more music, both old and new, to continue presenting the great music to WRUW\'s listeners. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Fat Monday','','inherit','closed','closed','','465-revision-v1','','','2019-04-08 00:10:09','2019-04-08 04:10:09','',465,'https://telethon.wruw.org/465-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3567,112,'2019-04-08 00:10:11','2019-04-08 04:10:11','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; WRUW has a long and proud history presenting the music of New Orleans and Louisiana.&nbsp; In past years you could hear it on \"When the Roses Bloom Again\" with Cuzin Dave, \"Annie\'s Blues Show\" with Ann Weatherhead , \"Rhythm &amp; Blues Survey\" &amp; \"Blue Monday\" with Walking Dr. Bill Anderson and \"Chanka Chank\" with Alison Kaslow Minor (One of the people responsible for starting the New Orleans Jazz &amp; Heritage Festival) as well as other shows. &nbsp; I have learned to love this music from these programmers and Ron Cass who started \"Fat Monday.\"&nbsp; </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> &nbsp; Your help during the 2019 WRUW Telethon will enable us to continue this tradition by adding even more music, both old and new, to continue presenting the great music to WRUW\'s listeners. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Fat Monday','','inherit','closed','closed','','465-revision-v1','','','2019-04-08 00:10:11','2019-04-08 04:10:11','',465,'https://telethon.wruw.org/465-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(3568,112,'2019-04-08 00:12:24','2019-04-08 04:12:24','