ompleted','closed','closed','wc_order_Tco9FBByFkOT5','order-apr-12-2019-0517-pm','','','2019-04-12 13:17:49','2019-04-12 17:17:49','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4686',0,'shop_order','',2),(4689,1,'2019-04-12 13:18:22','2019-04-12 17:18:22','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 01:18 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_e5SAocnCoAZlI','order-apr-12-2019-0518-pm','','','2019-04-12 13:18:48','2019-04-12 17:18:48','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4689',0,'shop_order','',2),(4692,7,'2019-04-12 13:19:12','2019-04-12 17:19:12','','iconic-playbills-graphic-hr-copy-01','','inherit','closed','closed','','iconic-playbills-graphic-hr-copy-01','','','2019-04-12 13:19:12','2019-04-12 17:19:12','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/iconic-playbills-graphic-hr-copy-01.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(4697,1,'2019-04-12 13:36:25','2019-04-12 17:36:25','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 01:36 PM','','wc-on-hold','closed','closed','wc_order_qJeAUWmZK8i2L','order-apr-12-2019-0537-pm','','','2019-04-12 13:38:32','2019-04-12 17:38:32','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4697',0,'shop_order','',1),(4699,1,'2019-04-12 13:44:48','2019-04-12 17:44:48','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 01:44 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_vKklDUfAhzpHB','order-apr-12-2019-0544-pm','','','2019-04-12 13:47:14','2019-04-12 17:47:14','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4699',0,'shop_order','',2),(4701,7,'2019-04-12 13:57:46','2019-04-12 17:57:46','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><b>Love showtunes and soundtracks?  So do I!  </b></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I grew up in Rockville, Maryland, near Washington, DC, and came to Cleveland to study at Case Western Reserve University.  I was a theater-geek in high school, working behind the scenes to build sets, run follow-spots, and play percussion instruments in the pit orchestra for <strong><em>Grease </em></strong>and <strong><em>Carousel</em></strong>.  My family attended local dinner-theater productions where we saw shows like <em><strong>The Unsinkable Molly Brown</strong></em>, and we saw National tours of <strong><em>West Side Story, Oklahoma!</em></strong> and others at the Kennedy Center.  We had a big collection of musical recordings at home and I grew up listening to all the famous theater composers.    </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When I came to CWRU, I got involved with WRUW as a sideline extracurricular activity to my studies in engineering.  I fell in love with the station, the people and the wide diversity of music.  I started hosting <strong>Sunday Matinee </strong>in September 1985, and have been serving up showtunes and soundtracks every since.  That means we\'ve been here for over 33 years.  (Yes, 33 years!!)  As host of the show, I\'m thankful WRUW has continued to provide a home for this music for so long.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whether you have been listening since the beginning (and there are a few of you who have), or just joined us in the last few weeks ... thank you for being a listener to<strong> Sunday Matinee</strong> <u>and the station that makes it possible</u>.  <strong>You\'re a member of a devoted niche of music lovers!</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>WRUW-FM 91.1 is a radio station based at Case Western Reserve University. </strong> Therefore, some people call us \"college radio\".  However, we serve a potential audience of over one million people throughout Northeast Ohio, so other people call us \"community radio\".  Regardless of what you call us ...<strong> we are a non-profit, non-commerical, all-volunteer and educational station</strong> with a mission to provide music, views and entertainment not generally found on other stations on the FM dial.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>As a non-profit, volunteer-driven station, we depend on listener support to fund our station operations.  </strong>In fact, as of 2018-2019, listener support makes up <strong><u>60%</u> </strong>of our annual budget.   You and our other listeners make it possible for us to buy new equipment to make the station sound better (and easier to operate), and to buy more music for us to play.  <strong>In other words ... ALMOST EVERYTHING you donate comes back to you through your ears.  </strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>The week of April 8 to April 14, WRUW 91.1FM is asking for your financial support. </strong>Your chance to support showtune programming and <strong>Sunday Matinee </strong>will be this <strong>Sunday, April 14, from 12noon-2pm</strong>.  If you don\'t want to wait that long, you can call us 24-hours a day (or donate anytime online if you prefer) and \"earmark\" your donation so it counts towards the show and music you love most.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>With your support, we can continue singing and dancing every Sunday, and kicking off your week with humor, good music, and songs to sing along with.  </strong>Thanks again for listening ... and donate today!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>David Caban<br>Host, \"Sunday Matinee\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Sunday Matinee Radio Show','','inherit','closed','closed','','511-revision-v1','','','2019-04-12 13:57:46','2019-04-12 17:57:46','',511,'https://telethon.wruw.org/511-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(4702,7,'2019-04-12 13:59:29','2019-04-12 17:59:29','','davidwruw','','inherit','closed','closed','','davidwruw','','','2019-04-12 13:59:29','2019-04-12 17:59:29','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/davidwruw.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(4703,1,'2019-04-12 14:00:50','2019-04-12 18:00:50','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:00 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_hxp1hPBJl80ha','order-apr-12-2019-0600-pm','','','2019-04-12 14:03:15','2019-04-12 18:03:15','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4703',0,'shop_order','',3),(4704,7,'2019-04-12 14:00:50','2019-04-12 18:00:50','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><b>Love showtunes and soundtracks?  So do I!  </b></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4702,\"align\":\"right\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"alignright\"><img src=\"https://telethon.wruw.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/davidwruw.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4702\"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I grew up in Rockville, Maryland, near Washington, DC, and came to Cleveland to study at Case Western Reserve University.  I was a theater-geek in high school, working behind the scenes to build sets, run follow-spots, and play percussion instruments in the pit orchestra for <strong><em>Grease </em></strong>and <strong><em>Carousel</em></strong>.  My family attended local dinner-theater productions where we saw shows like <em><strong>The Unsinkable Molly Brown</strong></em>, and we saw National tours of <strong><em>West Side Story, Oklahoma!</em></strong> and others at the Kennedy Center.  We had a big collection of musical recordings at home and I grew up listening to all the famous theater composers.    </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When I came to CWRU, I got involved with WRUW as a sideline extracurricular activity to my studies in engineering.  I fell in love with the station, the people and the wide diversity of music.  I started hosting <strong>Sunday Matinee </strong>in September 1985, and have been serving up showtunes and soundtracks every since.  That means we\'ve been here for over 33 years.  (Yes, 33 years!!)  As host of the show, I\'m thankful WRUW has continued to provide a home for this music for so long.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whether you have been listening since the beginning (and there are a few of you who have), or just joined us in the last few weeks ... thank you for being a listener to<strong> Sunday Matinee</strong> <u>and the station that makes it possible</u>.  <strong>You\'re a member of a devoted niche of music lovers!</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>WRUW-FM 91.1 is a radio station based at Case Western Reserve University. </strong> Therefore, some people call us \"college radio\".  However, we serve a potential audience of over one million people throughout Northeast Ohio, so other people call us \"community radio\".  Regardless of what you call us ...<strong> we are a non-profit, non-commerical, all-volunteer and educational station</strong> with a mission to provide music, views and entertainment not generally found on other stations on the FM dial.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>As a non-profit, volunteer-driven station, we depend on listener support to fund our station operations.  </strong>In fact, as of 2018-2019, listener support makes up <strong><u>60%</u> </strong>of our annual budget.   You and our other listeners make it possible for us to buy new equipment to make the station sound better (and easier to operate), and to buy more music for us to play.  <strong>In other words ... ALMOST EVERYTHING you donate comes back to you through your ears.  </strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>The week of April 8 to April 14, WRUW 91.1FM is asking for your financial support. </strong>Your chance to support showtune programming and <strong>Sunday Matinee </strong>will be this <strong>Sunday, April 14, from 12noon-2pm</strong>.  If you don\'t want to wait that long, you can call us 24-hours a day (or donate anytime online if you prefer) and \"earmark\" your donation so it counts towards the show and music you love most.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>With your support, we can continue singing and dancing every Sunday, and kicking off your week with humor, good music, and songs to sing along with.  </strong>Thanks again for listening ... and donate today!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>David Caban<br>Host, \"Sunday Matinee\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Sunday Matinee Radio Show','','inherit','closed','closed','','511-revision-v1','','','2019-04-12 14:00:50','2019-04-12 18:00:50','',511,'https://telethon.wruw.org/511-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(4706,1,'2019-04-12 14:02:10','2019-04-12 18:02:10','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:02 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_OJacCA4rL3zhw','order-apr-12-2019-0602-pm','','','2019-04-12 14:04:48','2019-04-12 18:04:48','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4706',0,'shop_order','',2),(4708,1,'2019-04-12 14:18:11','2019-04-12 18:18:11','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:18 PM','In Memory of Beyond the Pale','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_2pQfzIXiAG6r9','order-apr-12-2019-0618-pm','','','2019-04-14 09:43:41','2019-04-14 13:43:41','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4708',0,'shop_order','',5),(4710,1,'2019-04-12 14:20:51','2019-04-12 18:20:51','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:20 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_TVg0z1I0yaWA4','order-apr-12-2019-0620-pm','','','2019-04-12 14:22:23','2019-04-12 18:22:23','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4710',0,'shop_order','',2),(4712,1,'2019-04-12 14:45:48','2019-04-12 18:45:48','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:45 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_jjLTBuMqE7Px1','order-apr-12-2019-0645-pm','','','2019-04-12 14:48:04','2019-04-12 18:48:04','',0,'https://telethon.wruw.org/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=4712',0,'shop_order','',2),(4714,1,'2019-04-12 14:49:38','2019-04-12 18:49:38','','Order &ndash; April 12, 2019 @ 02:49 PM','','wc-completed','closed','closed','wc_order_1